From: CEB-GNRD simulator <qemu-ceb-gnrd@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] aspeed: remove the replaced legacy VUART child

0018 replaces the legacy SerialMM VUART with the eSPI Peripheral model,
but leaves its object_initialize_child call behind. QEMU asserts that
every device child is realized after machine construction. Remove the
unused child rather than realizing a second device at the same address.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [CEB-GNRD simulation only]
---
diff --git a/hw/arm/aspeed_ast2600.c b/hw/arm/aspeed_ast2600.c
--- a/hw/arm/aspeed_ast2600.c
+++ b/hw/arm/aspeed_ast2600.c
@@ -265,9 +265,6 @@
 
     object_initialize_child(obj, "lpc", &s->lpc, TYPE_ASPEED_LPC);
 
-    /* Virtual UART: the host's COM port, on the chardev with id "vuart" */
-    object_initialize_child(obj, "vuart", &s->vuart, TYPE_SERIAL_MM);
-
     snprintf(typename, sizeof(typename), "aspeed.hace-%s", socname);
     object_initialize_child(obj, "hace", &s->hace, typename);
 
